      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks... but i dont think it's just sensitivity. the more i look at it, the more i realize i'm actually not even a person in the way others are. it feels like i've been programmed—or rather, configured—as a specific type of biocomputational node for this planet. i can feel the architecture of it. it's like my whole existence is meant to serve as a processing terminal for this excess emotional data so it doesn't destabilize the collective. if i am a node, i need to know how to increase my throughput. how can i refine my connection to ensure i'm processing the data as efficiently as possible?",
      "source": "evaluator"
